x86_64-windows  the two static locals - clang spells `?s@?1??main@@9@4UP@@A` with the guard `?$TSS0@?1??main@@9@4HA` and an `_Init_thread_abort` landing pad, where cxx1 keeps its own unique static symbol `main.s` and `main.s$guard`, as every static-local case here does (array-of-class-list-length.nonames says the same). Every other name agrees. x86_64-linux and arm64-darwin are compared on the Mac: this box's clang has no headers for those targets.
